<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seven Sages of the Bamboo Grove</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">3rd century</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Seven Sages of the Bamboo Grove were a group of Chinese scholars and poets of the 3rd century, among them Ji Kang and Ruan Ji. They were known for drinking, music and philosophical &quot;pure conversation&quot; drawing on Daoist thought, and for avoiding service at a dangerous court. They became a favourite subject of later Chinese art and literature.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/seven-sages-of-the-bamboo-grove.jpg" alt="Seven Sages of the Bamboo Grove" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sesson Shukei · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E7%AB%B9%E6%9E%97%E4%B8%83%E8%81%96%E5%9B%B3-Seven_Sages_of_the_Bamboo_Grove_MET_DP361155.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
